{"id":"dag","ord":"a0","title":"DAG","desc":"Workflow TEMPLATES — the pipeline a lane walks, defined ONCE as a subtree.\n\n- Each step is a `todo` node; dependencies are `after` edges.\n- The app draws blocked-vs-ready, so the template is its own diagram.\n- `set_doing` refusing on a blocked node makes the order a refusal rather than a discipline.\n- **LAW:** never mark anything here.\n  - Dispatch CLONES a template under a new lane node in lanes.olai (real copies via `add_node`, one call with `children`).\n  - Then rewrites the `after` edges onto the clone's ids with `set_after`.\n  - Capture children cannot carry edges yet — the one wrinkle this prototype surfaced.\n- **Step ids:** `dag-<template>-<step>`; a clone keeps the `<step>` suffixes under a `lane-<task>-` prefix, so mark-flipping needs no search.\n- **Edge rule** the template must encode: a step that MUTATES the worktree sits `after` every step that READS it — readers fan out, writers wait.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T18:59:50-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr","parent":"dag","ord":"a0","title":"pr — implement through merge","desc":"The default pipeline for a dispatched PR lane. Facts the clone carries as properties: `agent`/`repo`/`item` on the lane node, `terminal` on implement, `pr` on the step that opened it.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-implement","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a0","title":"implement + open PR","todo":true,"desc":"Dispatch IS `set_doing` here. The clone's copy carries `terminal` as a property; `pr-url` lands when the PR opens.\n\nSPAWN SHAPE (graduated from instructions.md, 2026-08-25): the author spawns as a TOPLEVEL kolu terminal in a fresh worktree under `.worktrees/<name>`, in YOLO mode (`--dangerously-skip-permissions` for Claude), the agent chosen from the roster (agents-root; a name off it is not a choice). Everything through kolu — the discipline on Supervision is binding. Reviewers spawn as SPLITS, per their steps.\n\nTHE STAGE'S LAW (graduated from instructions.md — ir-pipeline-prose, 2026-08-25; CI sentence re-ruled 2026-08-29):\n- The author opens the PR with its initial implementation and NEVER merges it.\n- The author's bar at REPORT time is the LOCAL suites — typecheck, unit, the touched features, run serially and light. Never full CI at implement: CI runs ONCE, at the close step, by the CI WATCHER the orchestrator spawns after the review folds (dag-pr-ci carries the 2026-08-29 re-ruling; the verdict is always the orchestrator's read of the GitHub statuses, never an agent's claim).\n- The report ends at the PR URL @ head, and the author STOPS — no commissioning reviews, no merging, no board writes, kill by PID only.","created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T10:24:11-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-refactor","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1","title":"refactor passes","todo":true,"desc":"Only for a non-trivial, non-test-only code change — otherwise SKIPPED.\n\n- The author refactors its own PR, pushing each step as an isolated commit.\n- **Method:**\n  - architecture-first-principles (kolu's skill: .agents/skills/architecture-first-principles/SKILL.md)\n  - hickey (srid/agency .apm/skills/hickey) and lowy (.apm/skills/lowy) *together*, using human intuition so as to keep architecture simple\n  - /simplify when the author is Claude\n- These are method, not ordered sub-steps — one step here, deliberately.","after":["dag-pr-implement"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:04:21-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-merge-master","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a4","title":"merge latest master into the PR","todo":true,"desc":"A MERGE COMMIT, never a rebase. Runs ONLY when the PR has conflicts or CI needs code from master — otherwise SKIPPED. Sits after both reviews because it mutates the worktree they read — readers fan out, writers wait. Conflict hygiene is continuous: the orchestrator checks the PR still merges cleanly when the author finishes and again after review fixes — never discovered at merge time.","after":["dag-pr-review-a","dag-pr-review-b"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T19:49:47-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-address","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a5","title":"address findings","todo":true,"desc":"The author addresses the folded findings, given the PR comment link. No deferrals — the gate below owns the law; a finding that genuinely cannot be addressed here is a STOP-AND-ASK in the author's terminal, never a note in the PR.","after":["dag-pr-review-a","dag-pr-review-b"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-25T16:04:48-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-ci","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a6","title":"CI green at head","todo":true,"desc":"CI runs ONCE per PR in the happy path, after the review folds — and A DEDICATED CI WATCHER RUNS IT (the human, 2026-08-29, superseding the 2026-08-26 author-runs ruling): at close the orchestrator spawns the roster's claude-ci as a SPLIT of the author's terminal, in the author's worktree, briefed from orchestrator/ci-watcher.md. The watcher launches odu per its SKILL.md read in FULL (venue rulings bind from Supervision's ci-venue child; ONE venue per commit-status context) and follows the run step by step through odu's live faces (attach/wait/MCP) — NEVER a blind sleep. When the run settles it reports ONE message, two lists:\n\n- **FLAKES** — every test that failed at ANY point and passed on retry, named test-by-test with the observed values. The orchestrator ledgers each under `_olai/Inbox.olai`'s top-level `flaky tests` node and acts the flake policy below.\n- **REDS** — each genuinely failing recipe with its log path. The orchestrator routes these to the AUTHOR; the fix re-runs CI at the new head (a fresh watcher round — that run is the price of the finding).\n\n**THE VERDICT IS NEVER AN AGENT'S CLAIM** (the provenance stands: an author once reported `just check`-local as \"CI green\") — the orchestrator reads the machine truth: `gh pr checks <n> --required` must show an explicit pass on every required check, or mergeStateStatus == CLEAN. Never judge from the check rollup.\n\n**THE FLAKE POLICY** (the human, 2026-08-25; re-homed here 2026-08-29 so the boot chain carries the law — the Inbox node is the LEDGER, this is the LAW): a reported flake the PR does not own is filed one-entry-per-test-file under the `flaky tests` node and dispatched IMMEDIATELY — no triage lag. Several open at once = ONE lane fixes them all in a SINGLE PR. The author is pi or grok, never Opus. Auto-merge on review folded + CI green (the standing flake-class grant).\n\n**CodeQL ALERTS are branch-protection physics** (the human, 2026-08-26 ~19:46): ruleset 20608873 carries a `code_scanning` rule — ANY open CodeQL alert, any severity, blocks the merge — beside the ten required contexts; `gh pr checks --required` + mergeStateStatus is the whole gate.","after":["dag-pr-merge-master","dag-pr-address"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T10:24:01-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-evidence","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a7","title":"evidence verified","todo":true,"desc":"The author produces a screenshot (or video) proving the change working; the ORCHESTRATOR frame-verifies it before the PR is fielded. Evidence for terminal/visual work is photographed against REAL data (a busy stream, live padi) — quiet fixtures do not count as evidence.\n\nTHE RECIPE (moved here from olai's CLAUDE.md on the human's word, 2026-08-29 — evidence tooling is the orchestrator's to teach, not the downstream repo's): produce with a throwaway section at `.saatchi/evidence.ts` + `nix run github:juspay/saatchi` (shots land in `.saatchi/shots/`); upload with `nix run github:juspay/saatchi#publish` (paste-ready markdown block, video transcode included); details in saatchi's README — the recipe's one true source. Non-media artifacts or endpoint failure: Crabbox artifact publishing plus the manifest URL. NEVER push proof assets to any product repo branch; never commit `.github/pr-assets`.","after":["dag-pr-ci"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T10:41:05-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-deferrals","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a8","title":"deferrals ruled #human","todo":true,"desc":"HUMAN gate: a PR whose report carries deferrals merges only on the human's explicit word — **each deferral becomes a child of the `Deferrals` node in `_olai/Inbox.olai` first, carrying a `pr-url` prop naming the PR that introduced it** (the human's rulings 2026-08-28: deferrals park under the Inbox's Deferrals parent, never scattered across roadmap files, and every one links back to its source PR). A report that says \"no deferrals\" in so many words skips this gate.\n\nTHE LAW: a PR ships everything its roadmap item names and everything it spots in the code it touches — refactors of touched code, pre-existing hacks, review findings, nits. Diff size, noise, review burden, \"different shape\", \"wants its own PR\" are never reasons; neither is another repository's gate or a design question. What genuinely cannot be done in the PR is a STOP-AND-ASK in the author's terminal, and the orchestrator puts it to the human before the PR moves (overnight autonomy excepted). A `## Deferrals` section saying anything but `No deferrals.` is not merge-ready; \"filed as a follow-up\" counts as a deferral.","after":["dag-pr-evidence"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T19:16:11-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-merge","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a9","title":"merge","todo":true,"desc":"AUTO-MERGE IS THE DEFAULT: the pipeline completing — reviews folded, CI green at head (the ci step's explicit-pass bar), visual evidence frame-verified where the lane produces it — IS the merge authorization; the orchestrator squash-merges without a further ask. `merge-human` is the exception a ruling marks on the lane, honored absolutely.\n\n- Conflicts → the lane's author resolves them, then retry.\n- Multiple merges land in the order minimizing conflict work.\n- Before merging (or fielding a human-marked lane): read the author's FINAL message in its terminal; anything left \"for you\" is a STOP-AND-ASK, not a note.\n- Never file issues or act on another repo without the human's ratification. Only a URL or a roadmap entry counts as tracked.","after":["dag-pr-deferrals"],"created":"2026-08-15T19:05:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T19:49:56-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-retire","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"aA","title":"retire terminals","todo":true,"desc":"Kill EVERY terminal the lane spawned — the author too — and ONLY after the merge is confirmed, NEVER before: a green, reported, human-gated PR is still an OPEN lane, and a conflict round needs the author's live context, not a cold respawn. Applies to every lane shape. Reviewers MAY retire earlier, once their verdict is folded.\n\n- Verified against the live terminal list; executed in the SAME action block as the merge, never deferred.\n- Worktree removal is a SEPARATE step after the merge is confirmed — never bundled into the merge command.\n- After the merge the orchestrator syncs its own $PWD: `git pull --ff-only` (or `git pull --rebase` when local board commits predate the merge).","after":["dag-pr-merge"],"created":"2026-08-17T19:20:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T19:49:58-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-review-a","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1V","title":"review: first reviewer — named from the roster at dispatch","todo":true,"desc":"WHO reviews is never written here: the menu is the roster (agents-root's children; the clone's `reviewer` ref prop takes the choice, its step title takes the name — this template holds only the role).\n\nTHE STAGE'S LAW:\n- The reviewer reviews per HACKING.md and posts ONE PR comment — verdict + MUST/SHOULD/NIT at file:line.\n- Reviewers READ CODE: no suite runs, no CI, one surgical probe max, never edit/push/merge — the reviewer contract on agents-root is binding; gate verification is the orchestrator's.\n- Never two agents WRITING the same files at once; reviews are reads — fanning out is safe.\n\nSPAWN SHAPE: a reviewer opens as a SPLIT of the author's terminal, cwd the author's worktree — never top-level.","after":["dag-pr-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-25T15:59:19-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T19:50:07-04:00"}
{"id":"dag-pr-review-b","parent":"dag-pr","ord":"a1l","title":"review: second reviewer — named from the roster at dispatch (skipped when the lane names one)","todo":true,"desc":"Same law and spawn shape as the first review step — the roster names who, the clone's title takes the name, this template holds the role. A lane ruled single-reviewer clones one review step; pi-authored PRs clone BOTH (grok + Claude Opus).","after":["dag-pr-refactor"],"created":"2026-08-25T15:59:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T19:50:08-04:00"}
